    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nRedesigned the identity key to `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` and reworked duplicate detection around it.\n\n**`IdentityKeyDeriver.java`** (`mapper/`)\n- Changed `identityKey(telephone, email, householdId)` \u2192 `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)`, now returning the full **64-char lower-case SHA-256 hex** of `telephone|email|soundex(lastName)` (previously it returned a plaintext `a|b|c` string with `householdId`).\n- Added a self-contained **American Soundex** implementation (including the H/W adjacency rule and vowel reset) so no new dependency was needed \u2014 commons-codec isn't on the classpath.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Updated the `identityKey` mapping expression to pass `owner.getLastName()` instead of `owner.getHouseholdId()`, so the DTO's `identityKey` is the same 64-hex value.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (`addOwner`)\n- The **409 duplicate check** now compares the new SHA-256 identity key against each non-deleted owner's key (computed from their telephone/email/lastName). The email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`), and this single identity key is now the only 409 \u2014 no separate household-duplicate rejection.\n- Added **soft-match** logic: when no identity collision exists but a non-deleted owner shares the same `soundex(lastName)` **and** the same postcode (with a differing identity key), the new owner is still created (201) and flagged `possibleDuplicate=true`, `possibleDuplicateOf=<earliest matching owner id>`. This makes two owners with the same last name + postcode but **different telephones** a soft match rather than a hard 409.\n- Added `import java.util.Objects`.\n\n## Behavioural results\n- Same telephone/email/lastName \u2192 identical key \u2192 **409** (verified by `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`).\n- `identityKey` is `[0-9a-f]{64}` (verified by `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`).\n- Same lastName + postcode, different telephone \u2192 **201 soft match**, not rejected.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nThe existing `householdId` machinery (shared-household id, household size, level-ceiling capping) is retained unchanged; it's simply no longer part of duplicate detection.",
